<title>INDIA: Indian soybean up, oil steady, meal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean up, oil steady, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were slightly up on limited arrivals in central Indian markets on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Due to the rains, farmers brought their produce to market only in limited quantities. Business volume was dull and the undertone strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were steady in thin trading, with volume dull and the undertone easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were slightly down on poor export demand. Soymeal yellow was $305-306 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for exports. Rapeseed extraction was almost steady and quoted at $115 per tonne FAS in bulk for exports and was 3,900-3,950 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition.</p>
